  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved labour administration, social protection, wages systems and workplace compliance policies in Solomon Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Solomon Islands faces significant wage challenges, including low pay in unskilled and informal jobs, weak enforcement of minimum wage laws, and wage inequality across regions, skill levels, and gender. Many workers remain in subsistence or informal employment with limited access to stable income and social protection, while public sector wages are constrained by budget limits. Although overseas labour migration provides income opportunities, workers may face risks of exploitation.

To address these challenges, a capacity-building workshop on minimum wage setting is planned to strengthen stakeholders&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122; technical understanding of wage-setting principles, methodologies, and review processes, and to support the establishment of a Technical Minimum Wage Review Team. Following this, the Government is planning to undertake a comprehensive review of the minimum wage to ensure it is evidence-based, fair, and responsive to current economic and labour market conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
